[36m@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Git and GitHub Course Map[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis document tracks the practical implementation of Git and GitHub topics in this repository.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 1. Git Fundamentals[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Initialize a repository[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Configure Git identity[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Stage and commit files[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Check repository status[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Inspect commit history[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Compare changes with git diff[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Use .gitignore[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Restore and recover files[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 2. Branching and Integration[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Create the main branch[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Create the develop branch[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Create feature branches[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Merge branches[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Resolve merge conflicts[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Practice cherry-pick[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Practice rebase[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Inspect reflog[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 3. GitHub Collaboration[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Create a public repository[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Configure a remote[m
[32m+[m[32m- [x] Push commits to GitHub[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Create an issue[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Create a pull request[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Review and merge a pull request[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Configure GitHub Pages[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 4. Releases and Git Flow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Follow main, develop, feature, release and hotfix branches[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Create annotated Git tags[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Publish a GitHub Release[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Maintain a changelog[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## 5. Advanced Git[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Use git stash[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Compare commits[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Amend a commit[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Practice reset and revert safely[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Practice interactive rebase[m
[32m+[m[32m- [ ] Use git bisect[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Evidence[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPractical progress should be demonstrated through actual commits, branches,[m
[32m+[m[32mpull requests, tags, releases and repository history.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTopics are marked complete only after they have been practiced.[m
